  "deletedAt": null,
  "deletedBy": null,
  "details": "This is a issue occurred since months ago, and occurring randomly across different client versions. \n\nDetails:\n\n1. When join a new instance, loading avatars of other users, the frame rate will going down (usually less than 20~30) when downloading, and stuck for a little bit when unpacking. After everyone's avatar are ready, the frame rate will restore (for example, back to 60 or higher). This will going more worse when there is many users near by. \n\n2. The first time I occur this issue, is version 12xx. Since that, some release did fix it, some did occur again. \n\n3. I believe this is a mistake, and  when the download and main graphics workload are in the same logic processor, it will results the performance fallback and frame rate issues. \n\n4. Also, seems like the parallel download or multi-thread download were disabled in current client. Including world download, avatar download and yt-dlp plugin. I suggest to enable then for better experience.",
